{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Reject the Gibraltar Treaty and reinstate full frontier border security",
        "additional_details": "On July 15, 2026, the land border fence was removed and Spanish police were installed inside Gibraltar Airport with entry-veto authority on British soil. We believe handing a foreign state police jurisdiction over a strategic British territory during severe global instability is a grave national security risk. Parliament should vote against final ratification under the CRAG Act 2010, remove foreign police from British soil, and restore complete frontier border security.",
        "background": "We call on Parliament to exercise its powers under Section 20 of the CRAG Act 2010 to vote against final ratification of the UK-EU Gibraltar Treaty, remove foreign law enforcement from British territory, and reinstate full frontier border security.",
